{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356312-an-teng-question","id":1356312,"title":"An-Teng Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-12-21T09:45:44-08:00","id":1356312,"title":"An-Teng Question","content":"Trying to remember which of the Books of Terrestrial Directions had a write-up on the Southwestern nation of An-Teng in 2nd Edition... Vol. II (West) or Vol. IV (South).<br /> <br /> Hoping that when Across the Eight Directions comes out, it will have updated information on An-Teng for 3Ex.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T09:51:41-08:00","id":1356313,"title":"","content":"An-Teng's write-up would be in the Compass: South book iirc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T10:15:48-08:00","id":1356318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356312-an-teng-question?p=1356313#post1356313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An-Teng's write-up would be in the Compass: South book iirc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's correct. Chapter 8 (&quot;Flowers and Secrets&quot;) of Compass of Terrestrial Directions Volume 4: The South is all about An-Teng.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T10:18:22-08:00","id":1356319,"title":"","content":"Huh... I would have thought the West to be honest (that was the direction i was leaning towards). Sadly, I don't have access to my 2E books at the moment or I would just look it up. Just trying to decide if the information is worth buying the PDF on DrivethruRPG... or if I should just wait and hope Across the Eight Directions has information there. Would be nice if we could get a preview of the nations that will be getting write ups in the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T10:25:01-08:00","id":1356322,"title":"","content":"Or the 1e book, &quot;Blood and Salt.&quot; I actually liked Blood and Salt better than the CoTDs' depiction, but your mileage may vary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T10:27:21-08:00","id":1356323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowstripe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356312-an-teng-question?p=1356319#post1356319\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh... I would have thought the West to be honest (that was the direction i was leaning towards). Sadly, I don't have access to my 2E books at the moment or I would just look it up. Just trying to decide if the information is worth buying the PDF on DrivethruRPG... or if I should just wait and hope Across the Eight Directions has information there. Would be nice if we could get a preview of the nations that will be getting write ups in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a secondary goal of the writers for third edition is not to retread TOO much of the stuff from 2e, so it\u2019s likely that things that got a lot of detail in the compass will he mentioned in the Across Eight Directions, but it will go deeper into detailing new stuff. So if you want all things An-Teng all the time getting both will still service you well.<br /> <br /> Or as Alucard points out even all three books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T10:51:03-08:00","id":1356328,"title":"","content":"I liked how 1E tended to provide a lot of information and detailed a lot of things in the nations it covered, but only getting information on a single nation or two at a time, given the number of nations that existed, got rather expensive. While 2E's approach wasn't quite as detailed as 1E, it provided enough essential information and details on important locations to make it worthwhile... and balanced this with providing multiple significant locations within each of the cardinal directions (personally, I would have gone with eight volumes to provide more areas between the 4 main directions).<br /> <br /> I am hoping that Across the Eight directions will still provide a good amount of information on popular locations from previous editions in addition to the new locations introdueced in 3E. Some information, such as significant Satraps of the Realm were given write-ups in the Realm book, so are unlikely to be repeated in this book... but An-Teng was not among them.<br /> <br /> The main reason I am looking into this now (rather than wait for the new book) is because I am thinking of running a new Dragon-Blooded game in the jungles to the South of An-Teng (with this nation being the main staging area for the group). I think the furthest South they will be going will be the Fount of Mourning (the swamp that saw the death of an Infernal, Lunar and Solar back in the First Age and where the most likely location for the Autochthonian Incursion tends to happen... though the latter has yet to happen in this game). Just trying to get a basic framework for the campaign set up that I can modify when/if new information is provided.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T13:55:27-08:00","id":1356368,"title":"","content":"An-Teng is iconic enough that I'm sure it would be included, at the same time as I imagine it will not merely be a retread of existing material any more than The Realm was. Some differences in tone, emphasis, style, in combination with entirely new plot hooks, details of the society and characters.<br /> <br /> Shorter than Blood &amp; Salt, but not written like a fact book entry. More like the satrapies and Lunar Dominions, I should think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T14:42:27-08:00","id":1356374,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... the thing about The Realm is it changed a lot of things, because the Blessed Isle book didn't really present an interesting place to set games.<br /> <br /> Whereas the areas that have been described in detail in two editions (An-Teng, the Lintha, Harborhead, Lookshy, Halta, Gethemene, Whitewall, the Haslanti League) don't generally need big rewrites (maybe the Lintha and Halta, but not most of them).<br /> I've got Blood and Salt and Compass: South, I'd rather hear about some new stuff. A section on Goldenseal explaining how it and other Cinder Coast states interact with An-Teng should be fine.<br /> Nor do I feel An-Teng needs to be significantly changed for 3rd edition.<br /> <br /> Not that I am going to be really angry if they do a really good write-up of An-Teng... I'd just find something new more interesting.<br /> Admittedly, if over half the book was just rewrites of old places I have books about already, I would be a lot less likely to buy it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T15:47:58-08:00","id":1356383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356312-an-teng-question?p=1356374#post1356374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the thing about The Realm is it changed a lot of things</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to open a dialogue about this in order to explore the subject and understand one another's reasoning.<br /> <br /> That is the context in which I would ask what you see as having been changed about the Realm. I'm not saying <i>nothing</i> has been changed, but I think there's something to derive from the details.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whereas the areas that have been described in detail in two editions (An-Teng, the Lintha, Harborhead, Lookshy, Halta, Gethemene, Whitewall, the Haslanti League) don't generally need big rewrites (maybe the Lintha and Halta, but not most of them). I've got Blood and Salt and Compass: South, I'd rather hear about some new stuff. A section on Goldenseal explaining how it and other Cinder Coast states interact with An-Teng should be fine.<br /> Nor do I feel An-Teng needs to be significantly changed for 3rd edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it's entirely a question of need. Having been things that were written in prior Editions is both why they have my interest enough to want to see them again, and why I want them to get a fresh coat of paint to reinvigorate that interest.<br /> <br /> We do not merely have new locations (and entirely new takes on places such as Luthe, Mahalanka and the Nameless Lair), there is a new methodology towards writing places that I would like to see applied to old favourites.<br /> <br /> It also is a question of need, because people that own the old books are not the sole audience.<br /> <br /> The West for sure could do with some significant rewrites to reflect its new place of historical isolation and becoming an untapped frontier for the Realm and other interests. Skullstone's place as the principality of a Deathlord might do with some sprucing to bring them in line with the new take on Abyssals and the Underworld, but that might wait for a later book. I feel as though the Coral Archipelago warrants a revision to be a bit less arch while retaining the core characteristics, but that's a matter of personal taste. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T16:41:11-08:00","id":1356393,"title":"","content":"In terms of the Realm, its geography has been changed to be more varied, but primarily it's been crammed full of Anathema tombs, forests of monsters, valleys of spirits, etc, to give you plots to do besides Dynastic intrigue, as honestly the 2nd ed Blessed Isle didn't present much to do.<br /> <br /> Whereas An-Teng, Whitewall, Harborhead, etc, already had plenty to do (for their size).<br /> <br /> I see your point about methodology, and I can't see a rewrite of An-Teng hurting, but I would find using that word count for a new place in the South-West more useful and more interesting. (As to new players without the previous books, I don't imagine it makes much difference since it's all new, so why not do a new place anyway.)<br /> <br /> I think of all the directions (beyond the Realm) the West could do most with a rewrite, what with the changes to its context in many ways. Which makes me wonder if they are still planning to do the &quot;War in the West&quot; book, or just rewrite, say, Skullstone and Coral for Across The Eight Directions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T16:47:45-08:00","id":1356396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356312-an-teng-question?p=1356322#post1356322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or the 1e book, &amp;quot;Blood and Salt.&amp;quot; I actually liked Blood and Salt better than the CoTDs' depiction, but your mileage may vary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did too, but of course it's subjective.<br /> <br /> Shadowstripe, they've mentioned that Across The Eight Directions will have some old places, like Nexus (sigh), and a couple of new places were mentioned (such as a place ruled by Raksha). But they didn't give enough detail to say about An-Teng. Maybe they'll give more details closer to the time.<br /> <br /> Although you could just ask Robert and Eric if An-Teng is in on the Ask the Devs thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T16:48:58-08:00","id":1356397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or the 1e book, &quot;Blood and Salt.&quot; I actually liked Blood and Salt better than the CoTDs' depiction, but your mileage may vary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am with Alucard on this one. I mush prefer the way they treated An-Teng in 1e. Also, Blood &amp; Salt was my favorite 1e book. I remember shocking some of the Ink Monkeys on how the sun moved around in 1e since it was only detailed in B&amp;S.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800080\">I express my opinions, but YSMV; Your Stories May Vary.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\"><i>Formerly known as wyrmpuff</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12288-mal-akh","name":"Mal'akh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12288_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-21T20:10:31-08:00","id":1356422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1356312-an-teng-question?p=1356393#post1356393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of the Realm, its geography has been changed to be more varied, but primarily it's been crammed full of Anathema tombs, forests of monsters, valleys of spirits, etc, to give you plots to do besides Dynastic intrigue, as honestly the 2nd ed Blessed Isle didn't present much to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are present and significant, but in a sense also a bit peripheral. Untamed wilderness has a stronger presence in text sure (I'm not sure it was strictly absent in the past, but at best mentioned uncommonly and never built upon), but the core elements that are the history, the society, the administrative organisation and government, these remain largely the same in the broad strokes and in many of the details.<br /> <br /> Yet they're also written with a new kind of energy, with a focus on creating a dynamic sense of time and place, where off-hand details can imply plot hooks or ideas for how players might pursue some goal, and it gives the world a bit more sense of character.<br /> <br /> That and examining some parts that had weaknesses and giving them an overhaul while retaining the core features. The All-Seeing Eye stands out in that regard, having gone from what felt like something between watered down magistrates and just being the official name of House Iselsi into something with a lot more of the flavour of stale beer and some of that good old rogue CIA in South America/Southeast Asia or former KGB in actual Russia prospects in their future to oppose, hijack or take part in.<br /> <br /> Even among prefectures, you've got a lot of names and core concepts that have been carried forward, but upgraded from well-written but a bit dry and one note to more lively and vivid places. The Realm is more than the addition of tombs and forests to adventure in, it's the new version of Juche, a place that just off the top of my head brims with potential as a power base to safeguard and fund the ascension of House Nellens, an asset that their enemies can't afford to leave in their hands, and a core of the Realm's spirituality for Celestial Exalted to target for breaking down or appropriating for their own ends.<br /> <br /> ...Oh dang, between the wealth drawn in from pilgrims and its significance to Immaculate beliefs, I've only just realised that seeing more of Juche puts a whole new spin on What Fire Has Wrought depicting House Ledaal as having designs on the assets of their neighbour.<br /> <br /> And most of it written with a pretty decent economy of wording. I think I noted when reading Fangs at the Gate that Dominion write-ups managed to on average be shorter than places in Compass books, and that's without consideration for how the format in the finished product will make each of them take even fewer pages.<br /> <br /> My point is that I think there's a firm basis for setting how our current writers and development could take something familiar and trim some of the gristle while spicing it up a bit, and still ending up with something that takes up less space than it has in previous books.<br /> <br /> Give me a bit of time and I think I could identify some specific details that I think would benefit from that treatment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(As to new players without the previous books, I don't imagine it makes much difference since it's all new, so why not do a new place anyway.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it's neat and with sharing with new folks in a manner consistent with the format The Realm and What Fire Has Wrought has acclimated them to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}